  "area": "bahamas-new-providence",
  "method": "New Providence (Nassau, Paradise Island, Rose Island, the south-west Tongue of the Ocean wall and the film wrecks). No Bahamas National Trust dive-site list exists for the island, so the official stand-in is the tourism list, meaning the Bahamas Ministry of Tourism (bahamas.com dive, island, blog and natural-wonders pages) together with the Bahamas Diving Association pages it co-publishes (read through the Wayback Machine, 2005-06), counted as one list. Operator lists: Stuart Cove's Dive Bahamas (its site pages from the 2003 Wayback snapshot, whose English site names are legible, plus its current shark-adventure and dive-trips pages; the current dive-site page is a map image that archives without its image) and Bahama Divers (its 2012 Wayback diving page, the latest readable one; bahamadivers.com is now a blog and a default server page). Nassau Scuba Centre and Dive Dive Dive could not be read (nassauscubacentre.com archives only empty frames). The 2003 and 2012 snapshots predate recent sinkings, so a site counts only when it also appears on a second list; wrecks sunk after 2012 (Ray of Hope, Sea Trader) appear on the tourism list alone. A site counts when named, recreationally divable and on at least two independent lists; one-list names, the pelagic Shark Buoy and the 135-foot-plus walls are excluded with reasons. Counted 2026-10-14.",
